#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versi paket\">\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode di halaman ini dikembangkan dengan persyaratan berikut.\n"
"Kami menyarankan untuk menggunakan versi ini atau yang lebih baru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use this page to upload a workflow, run it, and get its result. The example workflow optimizes and simulates a Qiskit circuit. It simulates the circuit on classical hardware, so it does not use QPU time.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Gunakan halaman ini untuk mengunggah workflow, menjalankannya, dan mengambil hasilnya. Contoh workflow ini mengoptimalkan dan mensimulasikan Circuit Qiskit. Workflow ini mensimulasikan Circuit pada hardware klasik, jadi tidak memakai waktu QPU.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Before you begin, [install the client package and authenticate](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"
msgstr "Sebelum mulai, [instal paket klien dan lakukan autentikasi](/guides/install-managed-workflows).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Use AI skills (optional)\">\n"
"To deploy your own code with help from an AI assistant, use the AI skills in the [Qiskit Function templates repository](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Gunakan AI skills (opsional)\">\n"
"Untuk men-deploy kodemu sendiri dengan bantuan asisten AI, gunakan AI skills di [repositori Qiskit Function templates](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qiskit-function-templates).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write a workflow {#write-a-workflow}"
msgstr "Tulis workflow {#write-a-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create the folder structure {#create-the-folder-structure}"
msgstr "Buat struktur folder {#create-the-folder-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A managed workflow is a folder of Python files with one entrypoint file. A managed workflow uploads everything in the folder, up to 50 MB, and runs the entrypoint as a script. Because a workflow uploads the whole folder, keep your local files, such as `deploy.ipynb`, outside the folder. Create the following layout:\n"
msgstr "Managed workflow adalah folder berisi file Python dengan satu file entrypoint. Managed workflow mengunggah semua isi folder, hingga 50 MB, dan menjalankan entrypoint sebagai skrip. Karena workflow mengunggah seluruh folder, simpan file lokalmu, seperti `deploy.ipynb`, di luar folder tersebut. Buat tata letak berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Write the hello world entrypoint {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"
msgstr "Tulis entrypoint hello world {#write-the-hello-world-entrypoint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint reads a circuit, optimizes and simulates it, and saves the counts and two-qubit depth. Save the following code as `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"
msgstr "Entrypoint membaca Circuit, mengoptimalkan dan mensimulasikannya, lalu menyimpan counts dan kedalaman dua qubit. Simpan kode berikut sebagai `source_files/hello_world.py`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"If you read this page as a notebook, the code cell for `hello_world.py` starts with the `%%writefile` [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile). When you run this cell, it saves the code to the file instead of running the code.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\">\n"
"Jika kamu membaca halaman ini sebagai notebook, sel kode untuk `hello_world.py` diawali dengan [magic command](https://ipython.readthedocs.io/en/stable/interactive/magics.html#cellmagic-writefile) `%%writefile`. Saat kamu menjalankan sel ini, kode akan disimpan ke file, bukan dijalankan.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The entrypoint uses three functions from `qiskit_serverless`:\n"
msgstr "Entrypoint menggunakan tiga fungsi dari `qiskit_serverless`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`get_arguments()` returns the keyword arguments that you pass to `run()`, as a dictionary. Each value must be JSON-serializable, or an object that the client can encode, such as a `QuantumCircuit`. Encoded objects arrive as the same objects that you passed.\n"
msgstr "`get_arguments()` mengembalikan keyword argument yang kamu berikan ke `run()`, sebagai dictionary. Setiap nilai harus bisa diserialisasi ke JSON, atau berupa objek yang bisa di-encode oleh klien, seperti `QuantumCircuit`. Objek yang di-encode tiba sebagai objek yang sama dengan yang kamu berikan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` sets the detailed status `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, which you can see while the job runs. See [Report progress with update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"
msgstr "`update_status(Job.OPTIMIZING_HARDWARE)` menetapkan status detail `RUNNING: OPTIMIZING_FOR_HARDWARE`, yang bisa kamu lihat saat job berjalan. Lihat [Laporkan progres dengan update_status()](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows#report-progress-with-update_status).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`save_result()` stores a JSON-serializable value that you read later with `job.result()`. The workflow returns the counts as a dictionary and the two-qubit depth of the optimized circuit as an integer.\n"
msgstr "`save_result()` menyimpan nilai yang bisa diserialisasi ke JSON yang kamu baca nanti dengan `job.result()`. Workflow ini mengembalikan counts sebagai dictionary dan kedalaman dua qubit dari Circuit yang sudah dioptimalkan sebagai bilangan bulat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything that the workflow writes to standard output, such as the two-qubit depth, goes to the job's logs. To add timestamps and log levels, use the `logging` module. See [Write logs and handle errors](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"
msgstr "Semua yang ditulis workflow ke standard output, seperti kedalaman dua qubit, masuk ke log job. Untuk menambahkan timestamp dan level log, gunakan modul `logging`. Lihat [Tulis log dan tangani error](/guides/managed-workflow-logs-and-errors).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Upload the workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Unggah workflow {#upload-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In your local notebook, run the following code from the `hello_world_project` folder. The code connects with your saved account, defines the workflow, and uploads it. `entrypoint` is the file that the workflow runs, and `working_dir` is the folder that you upload:\n"
msgstr "Di notebook lokalmu, jalankan kode berikut dari folder `hello_world_project`. Kode ini terhubung dengan akun tersimpanmu, mendefinisikan workflow, dan mengunggahnya. `entrypoint` adalah file yang dijalankan workflow, dan `working_dir` adalah folder yang kamu unggah:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the workflow with inputs {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"
msgstr "Jalankan workflow dengan input {#run-the-workflow-with-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Construct a three-qubit GHZ circuit to pass to `hello_world` as an input:\n"
msgstr "Bangun Circuit GHZ tiga qubit untuk diberikan ke `hello_world` sebagai input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run `hello_world` with the circuit and the number of shots as keyword arguments. The argument names match the keys that the entrypoint reads with `get_arguments()`:\n"
msgstr "Jalankan `hello_world` dengan Circuit dan jumlah shot sebagai keyword argument. Nama argumen cocok dengan key yang dibaca entrypoint dengan `get_arguments()`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`run()` returns a `Job` after the workflow queues the job. It does not wait for the job to run. The job continues in the cloud after you close your Python session. To find it again later, list your recent jobs with `client.jobs()`.\n"
msgstr "`run()` mengembalikan `Job` setelah workflow memasukkan job ke antrean. Ia tidak menunggu job berjalan. Job terus berjalan di cloud setelah kamu menutup sesi Python. Untuk menemukannya lagi nanti, tampilkan daftar job terbaru kamu dengan `client.jobs()`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "{/* REVIEW: add the web UI for job history when it is available. */}\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Get the status, result, and logs {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"
msgstr "Ambil status, hasil, dan log {#get-the-status-result-and-logs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Immediately after you call `run()`, the status is usually `QUEUED`:\n"
msgstr "Tepat setelah kamu memanggil `run()`, statusnya biasanya `QUEUED`:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The status changes from `QUEUED` to `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, and then `DONE`.\n"
msgstr "Status berubah dari `QUEUED` ke `INITIALIZING`, `RUNNING`, lalu `DONE`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` waits until the job ends, then returns the value that the workflow passed to `save_result()`:\n"
msgstr "`job.result()` menunggu sampai job selesai, lalu mengembalikan nilai yang diberikan workflow ke `save_result()`:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/managed-workflows/deploy-first-managed-workflow/extracted-outputs/b4e7a2fe-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You can read the logs while the job runs. The workflow uploads new lines about every 15 seconds. The logs include the line that the workflow printed:\n"
msgstr "Kamu bisa membaca log selagi job berjalan. Workflow mengunggah baris baru sekitar setiap 15 detik. Log menyertakan baris yang dicetak workflow:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Update the workflow {#update-the-workflow}"
msgstr "Perbarui workflow {#update-the-workflow}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To change a workflow, edit its files and call `upload()` again with the same `title`. The new upload replaces the earlier one, and jobs that already started are not affected.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mengubah workflow, edit file-filenya dan panggil `upload()` lagi dengan `title` yang sama. Unggahan baru menggantikan yang sebelumnya, dan job yang sudah dimulai tidak terpengaruh.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fields such as `arguments_schema` and `sizes_map` keep their stored values when you omit them from the new upload.\n"
msgstr "Field seperti `arguments_schema` dan `sizes_map` mempertahankan nilai tersimpannya saat kamu menghilangkannya dari unggahan baru.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Langkah berikutnya {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"- [Define inputs and outputs](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) to learn which argument and result types a workflow supports.\n"
"- [Declare dependencies](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) to use more Python packages in your workflow.\n"
"- [Run quantum jobs from a workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) to run your circuits on a QPU, report each stage, and track the QPU jobs.\n"
"- [Run a managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) to learn all job statuses, debug a failed job, and find a job later.\n"
"- To start from working code, deploy one of the [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), or adapt a template for your own workflow.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Rekomendasi\">\n"
"- [Tentukan input dan output](/guides/managed-workflow-inputs-and-outputs) untuk mempelajari tipe argumen dan hasil apa saja yang didukung workflow.\n"
"- [Deklarasikan dependensi](/guides/managed-workflow-dependencies) untuk menggunakan lebih banyak paket Python di workflow kamu.\n"
"- [Jalankan job kuantum dari workflow](/guides/manage-quantum-classical-workflows) untuk menjalankan Circuit kamu di QPU, melaporkan setiap tahap, dan melacak job QPU.\n"
"- [Jalankan managed workflow](/guides/run-managed-workflow) untuk mempelajari semua status job, men-debug job yang gagal, dan menemukan job nanti.\n"
"- Untuk memulai dari kode yang sudah jalan, deploy salah satu [Qiskit Function templates](/guides/qiskit-function-templates), atau adaptasi template untuk workflow kamu sendiri.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
